# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Digital Twin AI — environment variables, common reference
#
# This is a documentation-only index, not a file the app actually reads.
# Backend (FastAPI) and frontend (Vite) each load their own local .env file
# independently — there's no single shared/merged .env in this stack:
#
#   backend/.env   ← copy from backend/.env.example
#   frontend/.env       ← copy from frontend/.env.example
#
# Never put backend secrets (DB URI, JWT secret, LLM API keys) in the
# frontend's .env — anything prefixed VITE_ gets bundled into client-side
# JS and shipped to the browser, i.e. made public.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── backend/.env ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MONGODB_URI                    MongoDB Atlas connection string
# MONGODB_DB_NAME                Target database name
# MONGODB_MAX_POOL_SIZE / MONGODB_MIN_POOL_SIZE
# MONGODB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS / MONGODB_SOCKET_TIMEOUT_MS
# NODE_ENV                       development | production
# JWT_SECRET_KEY                 required — app refuses to start without a real value
# COOKIE_SECURE                  Optional — defaults to NODE_ENV=production's value, so it
#                                 does not need setting by hand. Set explicitly only to
#                                 override that (e.g. an internal non-HTTPS production deploy).
# GEMINI_API_KEY                 AI assistant primary provider (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
# GROQ_API_KEY                   AI assistant fallback provider (https://console.groq.com/keys)

# ── frontend/.env ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_API_URL                   Relative (/api/v1) — routed through the Vite dev
#                                 proxy to the backend, so the browser sees the
#                                 frontend and API as same-origin (required for
#                                 the httpOnly auth cookie without local HTTPS).
